---
import { WorkflowIcon } from 'lucide-react';

import CardList from '@/components/CardList.astro';
import Card from '@/components/Card.astro';
import SubTitle from '@/components/Title.astro';

const TYPE = 'project';
---

<SubTitle subText="What I've been working on lately.">
  <WorkflowIcon /> Projects
</SubTitle>
<CardList>
  <Card
    type={TYPE}
    title="next-betterauth"
    subTitle="About"
    text={`
      I enjoy using Next-Auth for my authentication in Next.js, but you can't do many things
      with it. There is no register/signup at all within it and no way to track if a user
      has never signed up with you before. The aim of this project is to be a more flexible
      Next-Auth.
    `}
    githubUrl="https://github.com/zuice/nextjs-betterauth"
  />
  <Card
    type={TYPE}
    title="hono-tailwind"
    subTitle="About"
    text={`
      I was enjoying server rendering HTML and JSX with Hono (Express replacement)
      but one of my painpoints was that I couldn't use Tailwind unless I spun
      up a separate vite process on the side in development. So I built hono-tailwind
      to automatically compile tailwind classes for me using postcss.
    `}
    githubUrl="https://github.com/zuice/hono-tailwind"
  />
  <Card
    type={TYPE}
    title="jeffa.dev"
    subTitle="About"
    text={`
      This project is the site you're looking at right now. It's
      semi-statically generated with Astro (static with some dynamic bits).
    `}
    githubUrl="https://github.com/zuice/jeffa.dev"
  />
  <Card
    type={TYPE}
    title="Budj"
    subTitle="About (Currently private)"
    text={`
      This project is built with Next.js, tRPC, TypeScript, and Drizzle w/ Postgresql.
      It's a budgeting app for businesses in which they can track planned spend
      throughout their fiscal year. It's currently private, but if mentioned
      I'll be happy to share the code.
    `}
  >
    />
    <Card
      type={TYPE}
      title="edg.sh (Old)"
      subTitle="About"
      text={`
        This is a simple URL shortener I built a while back. It's built with
        Next.js and Node.js/GraphQL. The stack is a bit outdated but I think
        it still holds up well. I integrated with Stripe and used my hand-rolled
        authentication system.
      `}
      githubUrl="https://github.com/zuice/edg.sh"
    />
  </Card>
</CardList>
<small class="text-muted-foreground font-thin">Scrollable &rarr;</small>
